---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="about · devkage"
  description="About Bonaventura: MSc Computer Science with AI at the University of York, focused on HPC, AI, and ML."
>
  <article class="px-5 sm:px-6 py-6 sm:py-8 prose-post">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-block mb-4 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-tertiary)] no-underline hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)]"
    >
      ← back
    </a>

    <h1
      class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-[color:var(--color-text-primary)] mb-1"
    >
      About
    </h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[color:var(--color-text-tertiary)] mb-6">
      who · what · why
    </p>

    <h2>Who</h2>
    <p>
      I'm Bonaventura (Bona for short), Indonesian, based in Jakarta and doing an MSc in Computer Science with
      Artificial Intelligence at the <strong>University of York</strong> online. Before this
      I shipped commercial software in C# and .NET for a few years, mostly backend systems
      no one will ever see but a lot of people depended on.
    </p>

    <h2>What I work on</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AI &amp; ML</strong>: models, training, the maths under the hood.</li>
      <li><strong>Applied AI</strong>: taking models from notebook to something usable.</li>
      <li><strong>HPC</strong>: GPU kernels, profiling, sparse kernels.</li>
      <li><strong>C++</strong>: modern C++, RAII, the bits .NET hid from me for years.</li>
      <li><strong>LLM inference</strong>: KV cache, batching, quantisation. Why decode is slow.</li>
      <li><strong>MPI &amp; distributed compute</strong>: scatter, gather, reduce across nodes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why this blog</h2>
    <p>
      I share everything here freely because the resources that helped me the most when I
      was getting started were free, generous, and written by people one step ahead of me.
      I want to be that for someone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      No paywalls. No newsletter funnel. No "10x developer" thinkpieces. Just notes from
      the work, as honest as I can make them.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools I reach for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>C++20, Python</li>
      <li>Linux + zsh + vim, mostly</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Off the keyboard</h2>
    <p>
      Cafe hopping, gym workouts, a slow life, and reading books.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
